INSERT INTO `listening_clips` VALUES (1,'headway-001','Unit 1.1 — Introducing Yourself (Paula & Rosa)','A1','','Hello, my name is Paula. What\'s your name? Rosa. Where are you from, Rosa? I\'m from Chicago.',NULL,'[\"Paula\", \"Rosa\", \"Chicago\"]','Where does Rosa say she is from?','Hamburg, Germany','London, England','Chicago, USA','Paris, France',2,'Rosa answers: \"I\'m from Chicago.\"','Hello, my name is Paula. What\'s your name? Rosa. Where are you from, Rosa? I\'m from Chicago.','Paula giới thiệu tên mình và hỏi Rosa đến từ đâu. Rosa trả lời cô đến từ Chicago.',0,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(2,'headway-002','Unit 1.2 — Introducing Yourself (Richard & Kurt)','A1','','Hello, my name is Richard. What\'s your name? Kurt. Where are you from, Kurt? I\'m from Hamburg. Where are you from? I\'m from London.',NULL,'[\"Richard\", \"Kurt\", \"Hamburg\", \"London\"]','Which city is Richard from?','Hamburg','London','Chicago','Geneva',1,'Richard says: \"I\'m from London.\" Kurt is from Hamburg.','Richard and Kurt introduce themselves. Kurt is from Hamburg; Richard is from London.','Richard và Kurt giới thiệu bản thân. Kurt đến từ Hamburg, Richard đến từ London.',1,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(3,'headway-003','Unit 1.3 — Countries of the World','A1','','The USA. Spain. France. Russia. England. Brazil. Japan. Mexico. Germany. Hungary.',NULL,'[\"USA\", \"Spain\", \"France\", \"Japan\"]','How many countries are named in the listening?','Eight','Nine','Ten','Eleven',2,'Ten countries are listed: USA, Spain, France, Russia, England, Brazil, Japan, Mexico, Germany, Hungary.','The USA. Spain. France. Russia. England. Brazil. Japan. Mexico. Germany. Hungary.','Mười quốc gia được đọc: USA, Tây Ban Nha, Pháp, Nga, Anh, Brazil, Nhật, Mexico, Đức, Hungary.',2,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(4,'headway-004','Unit 1.5 — Rafael Ramos, Doctor from Mexico','A1','','My name is Rafael Ramos and I\'m a doctor. I\'m 30. I\'m married and I have two children. I live in a house in Toluca in Mexico. I want to learn English for my job.',NULL,'[\"doctor\", \"Mexico\", \"English\"]','Why does Rafael want to learn English?','For travel','For his job','For university','For his children',1,'He says he wants to learn English for his job.','Rafael Ramos is a 30-year-old doctor from Toluca, Mexico. He is married with two children and wants to learn English for his job.','Rafael Ramos, 30 tuổi, bác sĩ ở Toluca, Mexico, có vợ và hai con, muốn học tiếng Anh vì công việc.',3,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(5,'headway-005','Unit 1.6 — Yasmina Kamel, Student from Egypt','A1','','My name is Yasmina Kamel and I\'m a student. I\'m 19. I\'m not married. I have one sister and two brothers. I live in a flat in Cairo, Egypt. I want to learn English because it\'s an international language.',NULL,'[\"student\", \"Cairo\", \"international\"]','How many brothers does Yasmina have?','One','Two','Three','None',1,'She says she has one sister and two brothers.','Yasmina Kamel is a 19-year-old student in Cairo. She has one sister and two brothers and wants to learn English as an international language.','Yasmina Kamel, 19 tuổi, sinh viên ở Cairo, có một chị/em gái và hai anh/em trai, học tiếng Anh vì đó là ngôn ngữ quốc tế.',4,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(6,'headway-006','Unit 2.1 — Keisha Anderson\'s Profile','A1','','What\'s her surname? Anderson. What\'s her first name? Keisha. Where is she from? London, England. What\'s her job? She\'s a journalist. What\'s her address? 42 Muswell Hill Road, London. How old is she? 28. Is she married? No, she isn\'t.',NULL,'[\"Keisha\", \"journalist\", \"London\"]','What is Keisha Anderson\'s job?','Teacher','Nurse','Journalist','Dancer',2,'The speaker says she is a journalist.','Keisha Anderson is 28, from London, a journalist, not married, living at 42 Muswell Hill Road.','Keisha Anderson 28 tuổi, nhà báo người London, chưa kết hôn, địa chỉ 42 Muswell Hill Road.',5,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(7,'headway-007','Unit 2.3 — Patrick\'s Family Photo','A1','','This is a photo of Patrick, his wife, and his children. His wife\'s name is Brenda. She\'s a teacher. His daughter\'s name is Lara. She\'s 21 and she\'s a nurse. His son\'s name is Benny. He\'s 19 and he\'s a student. Lara\'s boyfriend is a nurse too. His name is Mick.',NULL,'[\"Patrick\", \"Brenda\", \"Lara\", \"nurse\"]','What does Lara\'s boyfriend Mick do?','He is a student','He is a teacher','He is a nurse','He is a journalist',2,'Lara\'s boyfriend Mick is a nurse, like Lara.','Patrick\'s family: wife Brenda (teacher), daughter Lara (21, nurse), son Benny (19, student). Lara\'s boyfriend Mick is also a nurse.','Gia đình Patrick: vợ Brenda (giáo viên), con gái Lara (21, y tá), con trai Benny (19, sinh viên). Bạn trai Lara, Mick, cũng là y tá.',6,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(8,'headway-008','Unit 2.5 — Dorita\'s Letter from New York','A2','','I have classes in English at La Guardia Community College. I\'m in a class with eight students. They\'re all from different countries: Japan, Brazil, Switzerland, Poland, and Italy. Our teacher\'s name is Isabel. I live in an apartment with two American girls, Annie and Marnie. They are sisters. New York is very big, very exciting, but very expensive. The subway isn\'t difficult to use and it\'s cheap.',NULL,'[\"New York\", \"Isabel\", \"subway\"]','What does Dorita say about the New York subway?','It is difficult and expensive','It is easy to use and cheap','It is closed at night','It is faster than buses',1,'She says the subway isn\'t difficult to use and it\'s cheap.','Dorita studies English at La Guardia with eight international students. Teacher Isabel. She lives with sisters Annie and Marnie. New York is exciting but expensive; the subway is easy and cheap.','Dorita học tiếng Anh ở La Guardia, lớp 8 học viên quốc tế, giáo viên Isabel. Ở với hai chị em Annie và Marnie. New York thú vị nhưng đắt; tàu điện ngầm dễ dùng và rẻ.',7,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(9,'headway-009','Unit 2.6 — First Day at English School','A2','','Hello, my name is Dorita. Hello Dorita, I\'m Orlando. Where are you from, Orlando? I\'m from Italy, from Rome. Good morning everybody. Good morning Sarah. How are you, Dorita? I\'m fine, thank you. What\'s your teacher called? Her name\'s Isabel. Is she a good teacher? Oh yes, very good, very nice.',NULL,'[\"Dorita\", \"Orlando\", \"Isabel\"]','Where is Orlando from?','Argentina','Italy','Spain','Brazil',1,'Orlando says he is from Italy, from Rome.','Dorita meets Orlando from Rome, Italy. Her teacher is Isabel, who is very good and very nice.','Dorita gặp Orlando đến từ Rome, Italy. Giáo viên của cô là Isabel — rất giỏi và thân thiện.',8,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(10,'headway-010','Unit 2.10 — Ordering Lunch','A1','','Good morning. Can I have an orange juice please? Here you are. Anything else? No, thanks. 90 pence please. Hi, can I help? Yes, can I have a tuna and egg salad please? Anything to drink? Yeah, a mineral water please. How much is that? Four pounds 95 please.',NULL,'[\"orange juice\", \"salad\", \"mineral water\"]','What does the second customer order to drink?','Orange juice','Coffee','Mineral water','Tea',2,'The second customer orders a tuna and egg salad and a mineral water.','First customer: orange juice (90p). Second customer: tuna and egg salad with mineral water (£4.95).','Khách 1: nước cam 90p. Khách 2: salad cá ngừ trứng và nước khoáng £4.95.',9,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(11,'headway-011','Unit 3.1 — Alison and Bob — Unusual Jobs','A2','','Alison is a scientist. She comes from Cambridge in England, but now she lives in Switzerland. She works three days a week at the Institute of Molecular Biology in Geneva. She speaks three languages: English, French, and German. Bob is a doctor. He\'s English but now he lives in Australia, in Alice Springs. He isn\'t an ordinary doctor. He\'s a flying doctor. Every day he flies to help people. He works sixteen hours a day, but he loves his job.',NULL,'[\"scientist\", \"flying doctor\", \"Geneva\"]','How is Bob\'s job different from an ordinary doctor\'s?','He works in a hospital in Geneva','He is a flying doctor who flies to help people','He speaks three languages','He works only three days a week',1,'Bob is a flying doctor in Alice Springs who flies to help people every day.','Alison is a scientist in Geneva, speaks three languages. Bob is a flying doctor in Alice Springs, working 16 hours a day.','Alison là nhà khoa học ở Geneva, nói 3 thứ tiếng. Bob là bác sĩ bay ở Alice Springs, làm 16 giờ/ngày.',10,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(12,'headway-012','Unit 3.3 — Alison\'s Languages','A1','','Where does Alison come from? Cambridge in England. What does she do? She\'s a scientist. Does she speak French? Yes, she does. Does she speak Spanish? No, she doesn\'t.',NULL,'[\"Alison\", \"scientist\", \"French\"]','Which language does Alison NOT speak?','English','French','German','Spanish',3,'She speaks French but does not speak Spanish.','Alison is from Cambridge, a scientist who speaks French but not Spanish.','Alison đến từ Cambridge, là nhà khoa học, nói tiếng Pháp nhưng không nói tiếng Tây Ban Nha.',11,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:08','2026-08-17 08:25:08'),(13,'headway-013','Unit 4.1 — A Busy Mother\'s Week','A2','','My weekends are fast and exciting. My weekdays are fast and domestic. I have two sons, Dylan, 7, and Dakota, 5. Every morning I get up one hour before them at 6 and I go to the gym. On Mondays I always go shopping and buy all the food for the week. On Tuesdays and Thursdays I visit my father. Every afternoon I pick up the kids from school. We never go out on Friday evenings because I start work so early on Saturdays.',NULL,'[\"gym\", \"shopping\", \"Saturday\"]','Why does the speaker never go out on Friday evenings?','Her children are tired','She visits her father','She starts work very early on Saturdays','She goes shopping',2,'She says they never go out on Friday evenings because she starts work so early on Saturdays.','A busy mother of two: gym at 6am, Monday shopping, Tue/Thu visits father, picks up kids daily, no Friday nights due to early Saturday work.','Mẹ hai con: gym 6h sáng, thứ Hai đi chợ, thứ Ba/Năm thăm cha, đón con mỗi chiều, tối thứ Sáu không ra ngoài vì sáng thứ Bảy làm sớm.',12,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(14,'headway-014','Unit 4.5 — Seasons in Canada','A2','','Al Wheeler from Canada: We have long cold winters and short hot summers. We have a holiday home near a lake, so in summer I go sailing a lot and I play baseball. But in winter I often play ice hockey and go ice skating. My favourite season is autumn, or fall. I love the colours of the trees: red, gold, orange, yellow, and brown.',NULL,'[\"Canada\", \"winter\", \"autumn\"]','What is Al Wheeler\'s favourite season?','Summer','Winter','Spring','Autumn (fall)',3,'He says his favourite season is autumn, or fall.','Al Wheeler from Canada enjoys sailing and baseball in summer, ice hockey in winter, and loves autumn colours.','Al Wheeler ở Canada: hè đi thuyền và chơi bóng chày, đông chơi hockey, thích nhất mùa thu với lá đỏ vàng.',13,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(15,'headway-015','Unit 4.5 — Seasons in Portugal','A2','','Manuela da Silva from Portugal: People think it\'s always warm and sunny in Portugal, but January and February are often cold, wet, and grey. I don\'t like winter. I usually meet friends in restaurants and bars. Sometimes we go to a Brazilian bar. I love Brazilian music. But then suddenly it\'s summer, and at weekends we drive to the beach, sunbathe, and go swimming. I love summer.',NULL,'[\"Portugal\", \"winter\", \"summer\"]','What does Manuela do at weekends in summer?','She meets friends in bars','She drives to the beach','She stays home','She visits family',1,'In summer at weekends she drives to the beach, sunbathes, and goes swimming.','Manuela from Portugal dislikes cold winters but loves summer weekends at the beach.','Manuela ở Bồ Đào Nha không thích đông lạnh ẩm, mùa hè cuối tuần ra biển tắm nắng và bơi.',14,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(16,'headway-016','Unit 4.6 — Introducing Jane from England','A1','','Hello everybody, this is my friend Jane from England. Hi, hello. Pleased to meet you. Sit down here, Jane. Do you like music, Jane? Yes, I do. Is it American? No, it\'s Brazilian jazz. Come and have a drink, Jane.',NULL,'[\"Jane\", \"England\", \"Brazilian jazz\"]','What kind of music are they listening to?','American pop','Brazilian jazz','Classical music','Rock music',1,'They clarify the music is Brazilian jazz, not American.','Friends introduce Jane from England and play Brazilian jazz music.','Giới thiệu Jane từ Anh và nghe nhạc jazz Brazil.',15,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(17,'headway-017','Unit 5.2 — Describing a Living Room','A1','','There are three people in the living room: a man and a woman on the sofa, and a little girl in the armchair. There\'s a radio on the coffee table and a rug under it. There\'s a cat on the rug in front of the fire. There are a lot of pictures on the walls, but there aren\'t any photographs. There are two plants on the floor next to the television.',NULL,'[\"living room\", \"sofa\", \"cat\"]','Where is the cat in the living room?','On the sofa','On the rug in front of the fire','Under the coffee table','Next to the television',1,'There is a cat on the rug in front of the fire.','Living room: three people, radio on coffee table, cat on rug by fire, pictures on walls, plants by TV.','Phòng khách: ba người, radio trên bàn, mèo trên thảm trước lò sưởi, tranh trên tường, cây cạnh TV.',16,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(18,'headway-018','Unit 5.3 — What\'s in the Kitchen?','A1','','This is the kitchen. It\'s not very big but there are a lot of cupboards. There\'s a new fridge and a cooker. What\'s in all these cupboards? Well, not a lot. There are some cups but there aren\'t any plates. I have some knives and forks but I don\'t have any spoons. Do you have any glasses? No, sorry.',NULL,'[\"kitchen\", \"cups\", \"spoons\"]','Which item is NOT in the kitchen cupboards?','Cups','Knives and forks','Plates','Nothing at all',2,'There are cups and knives/forks, but there aren\'t any plates.','Small kitchen with new fridge and cooker; some cups and cutlery but no plates, spoons, or glasses.','Bếp nhỏ có tủ lạnh và bếp mới; có cốc và dao nĩa nhưng không có đĩa, thìa hay ly.',17,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(19,'headway-019','Unit 5.4 — What\'s in My Briefcase?','A1','','What\'s in my briefcase? There\'s a newspaper, a French newspaper, and a dictionary, my French-English dictionary. I have some pens, three I think. Also I have a notebook for vocabulary. I write words in that every day. And of course I have my keys, my car keys and my house keys. There are some photos of my family. And there\'s my mobile phone.',NULL,'[\"briefcase\", \"dictionary\", \"mobile phone\"]','What does the speaker use the notebook for?','Phone numbers','Vocabulary words','Family photos','Train tickets',1,'He has a notebook for vocabulary and writes words in it every day.','Briefcase contents: French newspaper, dictionary, pens, vocabulary notebook, keys, family photos, mobile phone.','Trong cặp: báo Pháp, từ điển, bút, sổ từ vựng, chìa khóa, ảnh gia đình, điện thoại.',18,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(20,'headway-020','Unit 5.5 — Manola\'s Flat in Lisbon','A2','','Manola from Lisbon: I live in the Old Town near the sea, called the Alfama. I have a very beautiful flat. There\'s just one room, one very big room with one very big window. My bed\'s next to the window, so I see the sea and all the lights of the city when I go to sleep. I live alone but I have a cat.',NULL,'[\"Lisbon\", \"Alfama\", \"sea\"]','What can Manola see from her window at night?','The mountains','The sea and city lights','A busy street market','A large garden',1,'Her bed is next to the window and she sees the sea and city lights when she goes to sleep.','Manola lives in Alfama, Lisbon, in one big room with a window view of the sea and city lights.','Manola ở Alfama, Lisbon, một phòng lớn, giường cạnh cửa sổ nhìn ra biển và đèn thành phố.',19,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(21,'headway-021','Unit 5.6 — Asking for Directions','A1','','Excuse me, is there a chemist near here? Yes, it\'s over there. Excuse me, is there a newsagent near here? Yes, it\'s in Church Street. Take the first street on the right. It\'s next to the music shop. Excuse me, is there a restaurant near here? There\'s a Chinese one in Park Lane next to the bank, and an Italian one in Church Street next to the travel agent.',NULL,'[\"chemist\", \"Church Street\", \"restaurant\"]','Where is the newsagent?','Next to the bank in Park Lane','In Church Street, next to the music shop','Opposite the chemist','Inside the travel agent',1,'The newsagent is in Church Street, next to the music shop.','Directions to a chemist nearby, a newsagent in Church Street by the music shop, and restaurants in Park Lane and Church Street.','Hỏi đường đến hiệu thuốc, sạp báo ở Church Street cạnh cửa hàng nhạc, và nhà hàng Trung Hoa/Ý.',20,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(22,'headway-022','Unit 6.4 — What I Can and Can\'t Do','A2','','There are a lot of things I can\'t do. I can\'t drive a car but I want to have lessons soon. I can\'t speak French but I can speak Italian. My mother is Italian and we often go to Italy. My mother is a really good cook, but I can\'t cook at all. I can play tennis and ski. Sometimes we go skiing in the Italian Alps. Of course I can swim. I can\'t play any musical instruments. I love dancing. Of course I can use a computer.',NULL,'[\"Italian\", \"tennis\", \"computer\"]','Which language can the speaker use?','French','Italian','German','Japanese',1,'She can\'t speak French but she can speak Italian.','She can\'t drive or cook, but speaks Italian, plays tennis, skis, swims, dances, and can use a computer.','Cô không biết lái xe hay nấu ăn, nhưng nói tiếng Ý, chơi tennis, trượt tuyết, bơi, nhảy và dùng máy tính.',21,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(23,'headway-023','Unit 6.6 — Were You at Charlotte\'s Party?','A1','','Were you at Charlotte\'s party last Saturday? Yes, I was. Was it good? Well, it was okay. Were there many people? Yes, there were. Was Henry there? No, he wasn\'t. Where were you? Why weren\'t you there? Oh, I couldn\'t go because I was at Mark\'s party. It was brilliant.',NULL,'[\"party\", \"Charlotte\", \"Mark\"]','Why didn\'t the second speaker go to Charlotte\'s party?','Henry was not there','They were at Mark\'s party','They were ill','They don\'t like parties',1,'They couldn\'t go to Charlotte\'s party because they were at Mark\'s party.','One person was at Charlotte\'s party; the other missed it because they were at Mark\'s brilliant party.','Một người dự tiệc Charlotte; người kia không đến vì đang ở tiệc Mark.',22,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(24,'headway-024','Unit 7.1 — Maddie Smith\'s Daily Routine','A2','','Maddie Smith is 91 years old. She lives alone in Atlanta, Georgia. She starts her day at 7:30. First she has a bath, next she cleans the house, and then she sits outside on her veranda and thinks about her past life. Then she writes poems about it.',NULL,'[\"Maddie\", \"Atlanta\", \"poems\"]','What does Maddie do after cleaning the house?','She goes shopping','She sits on the veranda and writes poems','She visits her sisters','She reads the newspaper',1,'She sits on her veranda, thinks about her past life, then writes poems.','Maddie Smith, 91, in Atlanta: bath, clean house, sit on veranda, think, then write poems.','Maddie Smith 91 tuổi ở Atlanta: tắm, dọn nhà, ngồi hiên suy ngẫm và viết thơ.',23,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(25,'headway-025','Unit 7.2 — Maddie\'s Childhood','B1','','Maddie was never at school. She lived with her mother and four sisters. She started work when she was eight. She worked in the cotton fields from 6 in the morning to 10 at night. She couldn\'t read or write, but she could think and she created poems in her head.',NULL,'[\"cotton fields\", \"eight\", \"poems\"]','How old was Maddie when she started working in the cotton fields?','Six','Eight','Sixteen','Twenty-one',1,'She started work when she was eight years old.','Maddie never went to school, worked cotton fields age 8 (6am–10pm), created poems in her head without reading/writing.','Maddie không đi học, 8 tuổi làm đồng bông 16 giờ/ngày, sáng tác thơ trong đầu dù chưa biết đọc viết.',24,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(26,'headway-026','Unit 7.4 — Life in the Cotton Fields','B1','','I worked from 6 in the morning until 10 at night, 16 hours in the cotton fields, and I only earned 2 dollars a day. I married Hubert and soon there were six children. Hubert died just before our daughter Lily was born, 65 years ago. I looked after my family alone. I didn\'t learn to read and write until I was 86. Now I have three books of poems.',NULL,'[\"cotton\", \"Hubert\", \"86\"]','At what age did the speaker finally learn to read and write?','8 years old','16 years old','65 years old','86 years old',3,'She says she didn\'t learn until she was 86.','16-hour cotton field work for $2/day, raised six children alone after Hubert died, learned literacy at 86, published three poetry books.','Làm đồng bông 16 giờ/ngày lương $2, nuôi 6 con một mình, học đọc viết lúc 86, xuất bản 3 cuốn thơ.',25,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(27,'headway-027','Unit 7.8 — Memories of the 1990s','B1','','I left school in 1994 and went to university. I studied graphic design. In 1997 I got a job with Saatchi and Saatchi in London. In 1998 I met Zoe, my girlfriend. We bought a flat together in 1999. I remember when France won the World Cup in 1998. Tony Blair became prime minister in 1997. Princess Diana died in a car crash in Paris in 1997.',NULL,'[\"1990s\", \"Saatchi\", \"Princess Diana\"]','When did the speaker get a job at Saatchi and Saatchi?','1994','1997','1998','1999',1,'He got the job in 1997, just after university.','1990s memories: university 1994, Saatchi job 1997, met Zoe 1998, bought flat 1999, France World Cup 1998, Diana 1997.','Kỷ niệm thập niên 90: đại học 1994, làm Saatchi 1997, gặp Zoe 1998, mua căn hộ 1999, Pháp vô địch World Cup 1998.',26,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(28,'headway-028','Unit 8.1 — Great Inventions','A2','','Jeans: Jacob Davis and Levi Strauss made the first jeans in 1873. Television: John Logie Baird transmitted the first television picture on October 25th, 1925, in London. Aspirin: Felix Hoffmann invented aspirin in March 1899 for Bayer. He gave the first aspirin to his father for arthritis.',NULL,'[\"jeans\", \"television\", \"aspirin\"]','Who invented aspirin in 1899?','Levi Strauss','John Logie Baird','Felix Hoffmann','Jacob Davis',2,'Felix Hoffmann invented aspirin in March 1899.','First jeans 1873 (Levi Strauss), first TV picture 1925 (Baird), aspirin 1899 (Hoffmann for his father).','Quần jeans 1873, hình TV đầu tiên 1925, aspirin 1899 do Hoffmann phát minh cho cha.',27,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(29,'headway-029','Unit 8.3 — Did You Know?','A2','','Did you know that Marco Polo brought spaghetti back from China? Really? He didn\'t? That\'s incredible. Well, it\'s true. Did you know that Napoleon was afraid of cats? He wasn\'t. I don\'t believe it. Well, it\'s true.',NULL,'[\"Marco Polo\", \"spaghetti\", \"Napoleon\"]','According to the speakers, what is true about Napoleon?','He brought spaghetti from China','He was afraid of cats','He invented television','He made the first jeans',1,'They agree it is true that Napoleon was afraid of cats.','Surprising facts: Marco Polo and spaghetti from China; Napoleon was afraid of cats.','Sự thật thú vị: Marco Polo và mì Ý; Napoleon sợ mèo.',28,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(30,'headway-030','Unit 8.6 — Love on the Internet','B1','','I\'m quite shy face to face, but I find it easy to chat on the internet. I met Per there about a year ago on a chat line. We chatted for a year and exchanged hundreds of emails. Finally she let me phone her. She sent me her address, and one week later there was a knock at the door. I opened it and Per stood there with red roses. We fell in love and got married last Saturday.',NULL,'[\"internet\", \"emails\", \"married\"]','How did the couple first meet?','At a party','Through an internet chat line','At work','Through friends',1,'They met on an internet chat line and chatted for a year before meeting in person.','Shy Debbie met Per online, exchanged emails, phoned, met with roses, and married.','Debbie gặp Per qua chat internet, email cả năm, gặp trực tiếp với hoa hồng và kết hôn.',29,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(31,'headway-031','Unit 8.6 — Love in a Bottle','B1','','I love the sea. One day five years ago I was on the beach and stood on a green bottle. Inside was a letter in English. I couldn\'t read it then, so a friend translated it. A man in America wanted a wife. For a joke I wrote back and sent a photo. He wrote back immediately. We wrote every week for six months, spoke on the phone, and finally I flew to America. Now we have three children and a house by the sea.',NULL,'[\"bottle\", \"letter\", \"America\"]','How did Rosa and Vincent start their relationship?','They met at the beach','She replied to a message in a bottle','They were introduced by friends','They met at an airport',1,'She found a letter in a bottle and wrote back as a joke, which led to their relationship.','Rosa found a letter in a bottle, replied jokingly, corresponded for months, flew to America, married, three children.','Rosa tìm thấy thư trong chai, trả lời đùa, viết thư hàng tuần, sang Mỹ gặp mặt, kết hôn và có 3 con.',30,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(32,'headway-032','Unit 9.1 — Likes and Dislikes — Food','A2','','I don\'t like tea. I don\'t like wine or beer either. I like apple juice. I love all fruit. I hate all vegetables, especially carrots. My favourite meal is spaghetti, then ice cream. I like chocolate and chocolate biscuits. Everybody likes chocolate.',NULL,'[\"fruit\", \"vegetables\", \"spaghetti\"]','Which food does the speaker hate?','Apple juice','Chocolate','Vegetables, especially carrots','Spaghetti',2,'The speaker hates all vegetables, especially carrots.','Dislikes tea, wine, beer, vegetables; loves fruit, apple juice, spaghetti, ice cream, chocolate.','Không thích trà, rượu, bia, rau; thích trái cây, nước táo, mì Ý, kem, sô-cô-la.',31,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(33,'headway-033','Unit 9.2 — Offering a Drink','A1','','Would you like some tea or coffee? I\'d like a cold drink please, if that\'s okay. Of course. Would you like some orange juice? Yes please, I\'d love some. And would you like a biscuit? No thanks, just orange juice is fine.',NULL,'[\"cold drink\", \"orange juice\", \"biscuit\"]','What does the guest finally accept?','Tea','Coffee and biscuits','Orange juice only','Hot chocolate',2,'The guest wants only orange juice and declines biscuits.','Guest declines tea/coffee, accepts orange juice, declines biscuits.','Khách không uống trà/cà phê, chỉ lấy nước cam, không lấy bánh.',32,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(34,'headway-034','Unit 9.6 — The Strange Shop','B1','','Good morning, can I help you? I\'d like some orange juice please. Sorry, there\'s apple juice but no orange juice. And some milk please. Sorry, I sold the last bottle two minutes ago. Do you sell pizza? Oh yes, I do. Can I have pizza with cheese and tomatoes? Oh sorry, I forgot, usually I have pizza but not on Thursdays. Today is Thursday. What about bread? Yes, you\'re right, there isn\'t any bread.',NULL,'[\"orange juice\", \"pizza\", \"Thursday\"]','Why can\'t the customer buy pizza today?','The shop has no cheese','The shop doesn\'t sell pizza on Thursdays','The oven is broken','Pizza is too expensive',1,'The shopkeeper doesn\'t sell pizza on Thursdays, and today is Thursday.','Strange 24-hour shop: no orange juice, milk, cheese, or bread; pizza available except Thursdays.','Cửa hàng kỳ lạ: hết nước cam, sữa, phô mai, bánh mì; có pizza trừ thứ Năm — hôm nay là thứ Năm.',33,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(35,'headway-035','Unit 9.7 — My Favourite Food','A2','','Marion loves vegetables and Chinese food. Graham\'s favourite is a full English breakfast: bacon, eggs, sausage, mushrooms, tomatoes, and toast, especially on Sundays. Lucy loves pasta, especially spaghetti with tomato sauce in Italy. Gavin\'s favourite is Indian food — chicken curry with rice on Friday nights. Sally\'s favourite is chocolate — ice cream, biscuits, or a big bar of chocolate.',NULL,'[\"Chinese food\", \"English breakfast\", \"chocolate\"]','What is Graham\'s favourite food?','Chinese noodles','A full English breakfast','Indian chicken curry','Chocolate ice cream',1,'Graham loves a full English breakfast, especially on Sundays at home.','Five people describe favourite foods: Chinese, English breakfast, pasta, Indian curry, chocolate.','Năm người nói món yêu thích: đồ Trung Hoa, bữa sáng Anh, pasta, cà ri Ấn, sô-cô-la.',34,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(36,'headway-036','Unit 10.1 — Country and City Life','A2','','The country is cheaper and safer than the city. The city is noisier and dirtier than the country. The city is more expensive than the country. The city is more exciting than the country.',NULL,'[\"country\", \"city\", \"expensive\"]','According to the listening, how is the city compared to the country?','Cheaper and safer','Quieter and cleaner','More expensive and more exciting','Slower and more boring',2,'The city is more expensive and more exciting than the country.','Country: cheaper, safer. City: noisier, dirtier, more expensive, more exciting.','Nông thôn rẻ và an toàn hơn. Thành phố ồn, bẩn, đắt và thú vị hơn.',35,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(37,'headway-037','Unit 10.3 — Leaving London for the Country','B1','','Why did you leave London? You had a good job. Yes, but I\'ve got a better job here. And you had a big flat in London. Well, I\'ve got a bigger flat here with three bedrooms and a garden. It\'s cheaper and nicer. People are much friendlier here. The country isn\'t boring — Seacombe has shops, a cinema, a theatre, and a park. The air is cleaner and the streets are safer.',NULL,'[\"Seacombe\", \"garden\", \"friendlier\"]','What does the speaker say about Seacombe?','It is boring with nothing to do','It has shops, cinema, theatre, and park','It is more dangerous than London','It is more expensive than London',1,'Seacombe has shops, a cinema, a theatre, and a park — it isn\'t boring.','Moved from London to Seacombe: better job, bigger cheaper flat with garden, friendlier people, cleaner air.','Chuyển từ London về Seacombe: việc tốt hơn, nhà rộng rẻ hơn có vườn, người thân thiện, không khí trong lành.',36,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(38,'headway-038','Unit 10.8 — Directions to the Lake','A2','','Drive along Park Road and turn right. Go under the bridge and pass the pub. Turn left up the hill, then drive down the hill to the river. Turn right after the farm and the lake is on the right. It takes 20 minutes.',NULL,'[\"Park Road\", \"bridge\", \"lake\"]','What do you pass before turning left up the hill?','The farm','The lake','The pub','The river',2,'You pass the pub after going under the bridge, before turning left up the hill.','Route to lake: Park Road, right, under bridge, past pub, left up hill, down to river, right after farm.','Đường đến hồ: Park Road, rẽ phải, qua cầu, qua quán pub, rẽ trái lên dốc, xuống dốc đến sông, rẽ phải sau trang trại.',37,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(39,'headway-039','Unit 10.9 — Driving into the Lake','A2','','Well, I drove out of the garage, along the road and under the bridge, then past the pub, up the hill and down the hill, but then I drove over the river and it was terrible. I went through the hedge and into the lake.',NULL,'[\"bridge\", \"hedge\", \"lake\"]','What mistake did the driver make?','They turned left too early','They drove over the river into the lake','They missed the pub','They forgot to turn right after the farm',1,'Instead of turning right after the farm, they drove over the river through the hedge into the lake.','Driver followed directions but went over the river through a hedge and into the lake.','Lái theo hướng dẫn nhưng lái qua sông, xuyên hàng rào và rơi xuống hồ.',38,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(40,'headway-040','Unit 11.1 — Who\'s Who at the Party','B1','','Harry is a musician who works in LA. Mandy is very rich and lives in a beautiful old house in the country. Fiona is my oldest friend, a writer of children\'s stories. George is a pilot who travels the world. Rose and Sam are married and live in the flat upstairs.',NULL,'[\"Harry\", \"Mandy\", \"George\", \"pilot\"]','What is George\'s occupation?','Musician','Writer','Pilot','Teacher',2,'George is a pilot who travels the world.','Party guests: Harry (musician), Mandy (rich), Fiona (writer), George (pilot), Rose & Sam (neighbours upstairs).','Trong tiệc: Harry nhạc sĩ, Mandy giàu, Fiona nhà văn, George phi công, Rose và Sam ở căn trên.',39,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(41,'headway-041','Unit 11.8 — Buying a Shirt','A2','','Can I help you? I\'m looking for a shirt to go with my new suit. What colour? Blue. Do you like this one? No, it isn\'t the right blue. What about this darker one? Oh yes, I like that much better. Can I try it on? Of course. Is the size okay? No, it\'s a bit too big. Have you got a smaller size? That\'s the last blue one, but we\'ve got it in white. Okay, I\'ll take the white. How much? Thirty-nine pounds ninety-nine.',NULL,'[\"shirt\", \"blue\", \"white\"]','Which shirt does the customer buy in the end?','A large blue shirt','A smaller blue shirt','A white shirt','No shirt — it was too expensive',2,'There is no smaller blue shirt left, so the customer buys the white one for £39.99.','Customer wants blue shirt for new suit, tries one too big, buys white instead for £39.99.','Khách tìm áo xanh đi với vest, thử size lớn, mua áo trắng £39.99 vì hết xanh size nhỏ.',40,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(42,'headway-042','Unit 12.1 — Rosie\'s Future Plans','A2','','When I grow up I\'m going to be a ballet dancer. I love dancing. I\'m going to travel all over the world and learn French and Russian because I want to dance in Paris and Moscow. I\'m not going to marry until I\'m 35, and then I\'m going to have two children. I\'m going to work until I\'m 75 and teach dancing and open a dance school.',NULL,'[\"ballet\", \"Paris\", \"dance school\"]','What is Rosie going to do when she is older?','Become a pilot and travel alone','Become a ballet dancer and open a dance school','Become a teacher of French only','Retire at 35',1,'Rosie plans to be a ballet dancer, teach dancing, and open a dance school.','Rosie plans ballet career, learn French/Russian, marry at 35, two children, work until 75, open dance school.','Rosie muốn làm vũ công ba lê, học Pháp/Nga, cưới lúc 35, hai con, làm đến 75 và mở trường nhảy.',41,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(43,'headway-043','Unit 12.1 — Miss Bishop\'s Retirement Plans','A2','','When I retire, first I\'m going to learn Russian. I can already speak French and German. Second, I\'m going to learn to drive. Then I\'m going to buy a car and travel all over the world. I\'m not going to wear boring clothes anymore — I\'m going to wear jeans and T-shirts. When I return, I\'m going to write a book and go on TV.',NULL,'[\"retire\", \"Russian\", \"travel\"]','What is the first thing Miss Bishop wants to do when she retires?','Buy a car','Learn Russian','Write a book','Wear jeans',1,'First she is going to learn Russian; she already speaks French and German.','Miss Bishop, 59, plans to learn Russian and drive, travel, wear casual clothes, write a book, go on TV.','Cô Bishop 59 tuổi dự định học tiếng Nga, lái xe, đi du lịch, mặc jeans, viết sách và lên TV.',42,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(44,'headway-044','Unit 12.5 — Holiday Plans','A1','','First I\'m going to Holland. Why? To see the tulips, of course. Oh yes, how wonderful. Where are you going after that? Well, then I\'m going to Spain to watch flamenco dancing.',NULL,'[\"Holland\", \"tulips\", \"Spain\"]','Why is the speaker going to Holland?','To learn Dutch','To see the tulips','To visit family','To study dancing',1,'They are going to Holland to see the tulips.','Holiday plan: Holland for tulips, then Spain for flamenco dancing.','Kế hoạch nghỉ: Hà Lan xem hoa tulip, rồi Tây Ban Nha xem flamenco.',43,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(45,'headway-045','Unit 12.6 — Today\'s Weather','A1','','What\'s the weather like today? It\'s snowy and it\'s very cold. What was it like yesterday? Oh, it was cold and cloudy. What\'s it going to be like tomorrow? I think it\'s going to be warmer.',NULL,'[\"snowy\", \"cold\", \"warmer\"]','What was the weather like yesterday?','Snowy and very cold','Cold and cloudy','Warm and sunny','Rainy and windy',1,'Yesterday was cold and cloudy; today is snowy and very cold.','Today: snowy and cold. Yesterday: cold and cloudy. Tomorrow: probably warmer.','Hôm nay có tuyết và rất lạnh. Hôm qua lạnh và nhiều mây. Ngày mai có thể ấm hơn.',44,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(46,'headway-046','Unit 13.3 — The Burglars','B1','','It was about 2 o\'clock in the morning and suddenly I woke up. I heard a noise downstairs. I thought I heard two men speaking quietly — burglars. I phoned the police. The police arrived quickly and went into the living room. Then they came upstairs and said: It\'s all right now, sir. We turned the television off for you.',NULL,'[\"burglars\", \"police\", \"television\"]','What caused the noise in the living room?','Two burglars hiding','The television was on','A dog in the house','Wind outside',1,'There were no burglars — the police had simply turned off the television.','At 2am the listener thought burglars were downstairs; police found only the TV on.','2 giờ sáng tưởng có trộm; cảnh sát vào phòng khách và tắt ti vi — không có trộm.',45,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(47,'headway-047','Unit 13.4 — The Boring Story on the Train','B1','','On the train, a tall young man sat next to three children and their aunt. The boy Cyril whistled loudly. Don\'t do that, Cyril, said the aunt. She told a boring story about a good little girl. Why did they save her? Because she was so good. That\'s stupid, said the girl. When people fall into lakes, you save them whether they\'re good or bad. You\'re right, said the young man, speaking for the first time.',NULL,'[\"train\", \"aunt\", \"story\"]','Why does the young man finally speak?','The boy Cyril whistled again','He agrees the aunt\'s story is ridiculous','He wants to buy a ticket','He recognizes the children',1,'He says the aunt\'s story is ridiculous and agrees with the girl about saving people in lakes.','On a hot train, aunt tells moral story; girl and young man criticize it as ridiculous.','Trên tàu, dì kể chuyện nhàm; cô bé và chàng trai phản bác là vô lý.',46,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(48,'headway-048','Unit 13.5 — The Story of Horribly Good Bertha','B1','','Once upon a time there was a girl called Bertha who was always well behaved. She won three gold medals: Never Late, Always Polite, and Best Child in the World. The king invited her to his palace. In the woods a hungry wolf heard her medals clinking and ate her — everything except the three medals. That\'s a terrible story, said the aunt. No it isn\'t, shouted the children, it\'s the best story ever.',NULL,'[\"Bertha\", \"wolf\", \"medals\"]','What happens to Bertha in the end?','She becomes queen','The wolf eats her','She runs away from the wolf','She gives her medals to the king',1,'The wolf catches Bertha and eats everything except her three medals.','Bertha is perfectly good, wins medals, invited to palace, eaten by wolf — children love the story.','Bertha ngoan tuyệt đối, được mời cung, bị sói ăn — trẻ em thích câu chuyện này.',47,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(49,'headway-049','Unit 13.6 — Trains Oxford to Bristol','A2','','Trains from Oxford to Bristol Temple Meads, Monday to Friday. Departure 08:16 arriving 09:46. Departure 09:45 arriving 11:14. Departure 10:40 arriving 12:08. Departure 11:13 arriving 13:41.',NULL,'[\"Oxford\", \"Bristol\", \"08:16\"]','What time does the 08:16 train from Oxford arrive in Bristol?','09:46','11:14','12:08','13:41',0,'The 08:16 departure arrives at 09:46.','Oxford–Bristol weekday trains: 08:16→09:46, 09:45→11:14, 10:40→12:08, 11:13→13:41.','Tàu Oxford–Bristol ngày thường: 08:16→09:46, 09:45→11:14, 10:40→12:08, 11:13→13:41.',48,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(50,'headway-050','Unit 13.7 — Return Trains Bristol to Oxford','A2','','Good morning. Can you tell me the times of trains from Bristol back to Oxford please? About 5 o\'clock this afternoon. There\'s a train at 5:28, then the next one at 6:50. The 5:28 gets into Oxford at 6:54, and the 6:50 gets in at 8:10.',NULL,'[\"Bristol\", \"Oxford\", \"5:28\"]','If you take the 5:28 train from Bristol, what time do you arrive in Oxford?','5:54','6:54','8:10','6:50',1,'The 5:28 train arrives in Oxford at 6:54.','Afternoon return Bristol→Oxford: 17:28→18:54, next train 18:50→20:10.','Chiều về Bristol→Oxford: 17:28 đến 18:54, chuyến tiếp 18:50 đến 20:10.',49,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(51,'headway-051','Unit 13.8 — Buying a Train Ticket','A1','','Hello, a return to Bristol please. Day return or period return? A day return. How do you want to pay? Cash please. That\'s 18 pounds. Here\'s a 20 pound note. Here\'s your change and your ticket. Thank you. Which platform is it? Platform 1 over there.',NULL,'[\"Bristol\", \"day return\", \"Platform 1\"]','How much does the day return ticket to Bristol cost?','£10','£18','£20','£28',1,'The ticket costs £18; the customer pays with a £20 note.','Day return to Bristol £18, paid cash with £20, platform 1.','Vé khứ hồi trong ngày đến Bristol £18, trả tiền mặt £20, sân ga 1.',50,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(52,'headway-052','Unit 14.1 — Countries I Have Visited','A1','','I\'ve been to Germany. I haven\'t been to France. I\'ve been to the USA. I\'ve never been to Australia. I haven\'t been to any of the countries in South America.',NULL,'[\"Germany\", \"USA\", \"Australia\"]','Which country has the speaker NOT visited?','Germany','The USA','France','None — they visited all three',2,'They have been to Germany and the USA but haven\'t been to France.','Speaker visited Germany and USA, never Australia or South America, not France.','Đã đến Đức và Mỹ, chưa đến Pháp, Úc hay Nam Mỹ.',51,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(53,'headway-053','Unit 14.2 — Have You Ever Been to Paris?','A1','','Have you ever been to Paris? No, I haven\'t. Have you ever been to Berlin? Yes, I have. When did you go? Two years ago.',NULL,'[\"Paris\", \"Berlin\", \"ever\"]','When did the speaker go to Berlin?','Last month','Two years ago','Five years ago','They have never been',1,'They have been to Berlin and went two years ago.','Never been to Paris; visited Berlin two years ago.','Chưa đến Paris; đã đến Berlin hai năm trước.',52,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(54,'headway-054','Unit 14.3 — Life Experiences','B1','','Yes, I\'ve lived in a foreign country, in Japan. I lived in Osaka for a year and loved the food. I worked for Nissan, the car company. Have I stayed in an expensive hotel? No, never — only cheap hotels. But I have flown in a jumbo jet four or five times. I\'ve never cooked a meal for a lot of people. I\'ve never won a competition.',NULL,'[\"Japan\", \"Nissan\", \"jumbo jet\"]','Which statement is true about the speaker?','They have never lived abroad','They worked for Nissan in Japan','They always stay in expensive hotels','They often win competitions',1,'They lived in Osaka, Japan and worked for Nissan.','Lived in Osaka one year, worked for Nissan, cheap hotels only, flown jumbo jet 4–5 times, never won competitions.','Sống Osaka một năm, làm Nissan, chỉ ở khách sạn rẻ, bay jumbo 4–5 lần, chưa thắng cuộc thi nào.',53,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(55,'headway-055','Unit 14.4 — A Trip to London','B1','','We\'re having a great time. We\'ve been to Buckingham Palace — that was the first thing we did. We\'ve had a boat ride on the River Thames past the Houses of Parliament and Big Ben. We went on the London Eye. Tomorrow we\'re going to see the crown jewels in the Tower of London. We\'ve travelled on a double-decker bus and sat upstairs. On our last night we\'re going to the theatre.',NULL,'[\"Buckingham Palace\", \"Thames\", \"London Eye\"]','What was the first place they visited in London?','The Tower of London','Buckingham Palace','Harrods','The theatre',1,'Buckingham Palace was the first thing they did in London.','London trip: Buckingham Palace first, Thames boat, Big Ben, London Eye, crown jewels tomorrow, double-decker bus, theatre last night.','Du lịch London: Buckingham Palace đầu tiên, thuyền trên Thames, Big Ben, London Eye, ngày mai xem ngọc ở Tower.',54,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(56,'headway-056','Unit 14.6 — Airport Announcements','A2','','British Airways flight BA 516 to Geneva boarding at Gate 4. Last call flight BA 516 to Geneva. Scandinavian Airlines flight SK 832 to Frankfurt is delayed one hour. Air France flight AF 472 to Amsterdam is now boarding at Gate 17. Lufthansa flight LH 309 to Miami is boarding at Gate 32.',NULL,'[\"Geneva\", \"Frankfurt\", \"Gate 17\"]','Which flight is boarding at Gate 17?','BA 516 to Geneva','SK 832 to Frankfurt','AF 472 to Amsterdam','LH 309 to Miami',2,'Air France flight AF 472 to Amsterdam is boarding at Gate 17.','Airport announcements: BA516 Gate 4, SK832 delayed, AF472 Gate 17, LH309 Gate 32.','Thông báo sân bay: BA516 cổng 4, SK832 trễ, AF472 cổng 17, LH309 cổng 32.',55,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(57,'headway-057','Unit 14.7 — At the Airport','A2','','BA 516 to Geneva, that\'s our flight. Did the announcement say Gate 4 or 14? I think it said four. Look, there it is on the departure board — Gate 4. Can I have your ticket please? Just one suitcase. Can I have a seat next to the window? Yes, that\'s OK. Here\'s your boarding pass. Have a nice flight.',NULL,'[\"Geneva\", \"Gate 4\", \"window seat\"]','Which gate do the passengers go to?','Gate 14','Gate 4','Gate 17','Gate 32',1,'The departure board shows Gate 4 for their Geneva flight.','Couple confirm Gate 4 for Geneva flight, check in one suitcase, get window seat and boarding pass.','Xác nhận cổng 4 chuyến Geneva, một vali, ghế cửa sổ, nhận thẻ lên máy bay.',56,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(58,'cafe-order','At the café','A2','','Good morning. Welcome to Sunny Café. What would you like today? I\'d like a medium latte, please. Would you like anything else? Yes, a blueberry muffin. That will be eight dollars fifty. Here you go. Thank you!',NULL,'[\"latte\", \"muffin\", \"order\"]','What does the customer order?','Tea and cake','Latte and muffin','Espresso only','Sandwich and juice',1,'The customer asks for a medium latte and a blueberry muffin.','Good morning. Welcome to Sunny Café. What would you like today? I\'d like a medium latte, please. Would you like anything else? Yes, a blueberry muffin. That will be eight dollars fifty. Here you go. Thank you!','Chào buổi sáng. Chào mừng đến Sunny Café. Hôm nay bạn muốn gì? Tôi muốn một ly latte size vừa. Bạn có muốn thêm gì không? Có, một bánh muffin việt quất. Tổng cộng tám đô năm mươi cent. Đây ạ. Cảm ơn!',57,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(59,'airport-gate','Airport announcement','B1','','Attention passengers. Flight BA two four seven to London is now boarding at gate twelve. Please have your boarding pass and passport ready. Final boarding will begin in fifteen minutes.',NULL,'[\"boarding\", \"gate\", \"passport\"]','Where should passengers go?','Gate ten','Gate twelve','Baggage claim','Check-in desk',1,'The announcement says boarding is at gate twelve.','Attention passengers. Flight BA two four seven to London is now boarding at gate twelve. Please have your boarding pass and passport ready. Final boarding will begin in fifteen minutes.','Thông báo đến hành khách. Chuyến bay BA 247 đến London đang lên máy bay tại cổng mười hai. Vui lòng chuẩn bị thẻ lên máy bay và hộ chiếu. Lên máy bay lần cuối sẽ bắt đầu sau mười lăm phút.',58,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(60,'meeting-schedule','Team meeting','B1','','Hi everyone. Let\'s start the weekly sync. First, design will share mockups on Friday. Engineering needs two more days for the API. Marketing launches the campaign next Monday. Any questions?',NULL,'[\"design\", \"API\", \"campaign\"]','When does marketing launch the campaign?','This Friday','Next Monday','Tomorrow','Next month',1,'Marketing launches the campaign next Monday.','Hi everyone. Let\'s start the weekly sync. First, design will share mockups on Friday. Engineering needs two more days for the API. Marketing launches the campaign next Monday. Any questions?','Chào mọi người. Bắt đầu buổi họp tuần nhé. Trước hết, team design sẽ chia sẻ mockup vào thứ Sáu. Engineering cần thêm hai ngày cho API. Marketing ra mắt chiến dịch vào thứ Hai tuần sau. Có câu hỏi nào không?',59,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(61,'doctor-visit','Doctor visit','A2','','How have you been feeling? I\'ve had a sore throat for three days. Do you have a fever? A little, around thirty seven five. I\'ll prescribe some medicine. Drink warm water and rest.',NULL,'[\"sore throat\", \"fever\", \"medicine\"]','What symptom does the patient mention first?','Headache','Sore throat','Back pain','Cough',1,'The patient says they\'ve had a sore throat for three days.','How have you been feeling? I\'ve had a sore throat for three days. Do you have a fever? A little, around thirty seven five. I\'ll prescribe some medicine. Drink warm water and rest.','Dạo này bạn thấy thế nào? Tôi bị đau họng ba ngày rồi. Bạn có sốt không? Có chút, khoảng 37,5 độ. Tôi sẽ kê thuốc. Uống nước ấm và nghỉ ngơi nhé.',60,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(62,'hotel-checkin','Hotel check-in','A2','','Good evening. I have a reservation under Nguyen. Yes, a double room for two nights. Breakfast is from seven to ten. Your room is on the fourth floor, room four zero eight.',NULL,'[\"reservation\", \"breakfast\", \"room\"]','Which room is the guest assigned?','Room 408','Room 418','Room 308','Room 480',0,'The receptionist says room four zero eight (408).','Good evening. I have a reservation under Nguyen. Yes, a double room for two nights. Breakfast is from seven to ten. Your room is on the fourth floor, room four zero eight.','Chào buổi tối. Tôi có đặt phòng tên Nguyễn. Vâng, phòng đôi hai đêm. Bữa sáng từ bảy đến mười giờ. Phòng của bạn ở tầng bốn, phòng 408.',61,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09'),(63,'weather-forecast','Weather forecast','B1','','Today\'s forecast: cloudy in the morning with light rain after noon. Temperatures between twenty two and twenty eight degrees. Take an umbrella if you go out this afternoon.',NULL,'[\"rain\", \"cloudy\", \"umbrella\"]','What should you bring this afternoon?','Sunglasses','An umbrella','A jacket','A hat',1,'The forecast advises taking an umbrella if you go out this afternoon.','Today\'s forecast: cloudy in the morning with light rain after noon. Temperatures between twenty two and twenty eight degrees. Take an umbrella if you go out this afternoon.','Dự báo hôm nay: sáng nhiều mây, chiều mưa nhẹ. Nhiệt độ từ 22 đến 28 độ. Mang theo ô nếu bạn ra ngoài chiều nay.',62,1,'2026-08-17 08:25:09','2026-08-17 08:25:09');
